{
  "title": "31: Luqman لقمان",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ ‌ۚ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM MEEM.\nAlif, Lam, Meem. (A. L. M.)\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْحَكِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE HAKEEM.\nThese are the verses of the Book of wisdom,\nهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّلْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(3)\nHODAM WA RAHMATAL LLELMUHSENEENA.\nA guidance and a mercy unto the righteous ones,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوْقِنُوْنَؕ‏(4)\nLAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM YOOQENOON.\nThose who establish prayer and pay the poor-rate, and they, of the hereafter are certain;\nاُولٰٓئِكَ عَلٰى هُدًى مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(5)\nOOLAAA-EKA A’LAA HODAM MIN RABBEHIM WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThese are on the guidance from their Lord, and these are they who are successful.\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّشْتَرِىْ لَهْوَ الْحَدِيْثِ لِيُضِلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ‌ۖ وَّيَتَّخِذَهَا هُزُوًا ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(6)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYASHTAREAA LAHWA HAAZAL LEEZELLA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WWAYATTAKHEZAHAA HOZOWANW OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd of the people there is he who buyeth for a vain story, that he may lead (others) astray from the path of God without knowledge; and taketh it (the revelation from God) for a mockery; for these shall be a disgracing chastisement.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ اٰيٰتُنَا وَلّٰى مُسْتَكْبِرًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَسْمَعْهَا كَاَنَّ فِىْۤ اُذُنَيْهِ وَقْرًا‌ۚ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِعَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(7)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATONAA WALLAA MUSTAKBERAN KA-AN LAM YASMAA’HAA KA-ANNAL FEE AUZUNAYHE WAQRAN BE BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nAnd when are recited unto him Our signs, he turneth back proudly as if he had heard them not, as though in his ears were a heaviness; so give thou unto him the tidings of a painful chastisement.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(8)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANUT AAMANOO SAALEHAATE LAHUM JANNAATU NA-E’EM.\nVerily those who believe and do good, for them are the gardens bountiful,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(9)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQAN WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nTo dwell therein; It is the promise of God, (a) true (promise); and He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.\nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا‌ وَاَ لْقٰى فِى الْاَرْضِ رَوَاسِىَ اَنْ تَمِيْدَ بِكُمْ وَبَثَّ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ دَآ بَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍ كَرِيْمٍ‏(10)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE BEGHAYRIL A’MADIM TARAWNAHAA WA LQAA FIL ARZE JA-A’LA AN TAMEEDA BEKUM WA BASSA FEEHAA MIN KULLE DAABBATINW WA WA ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-ANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN KAREEM.\nCreated He the heavens without pillars as ye can see them, and He did cast mountains upon the earth lest it shaketh with you, and He hath spread in it of every kind of animals; and We sent down water from the heaven, then caused We to grow up therein (vegetables) of every noble kind.\nهٰذَا خَلْقُ اللّٰهِ فَاَرُوْنِىْ مَاذَا خَلَقَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ‌ؕ بَلِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(11)\nHAAZAA KHALQUS LAAHE FAAROONEAA MAA KHALAQAL LAZEENA MIN DOONEH BALIL ZAALEMOON FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nThis is the creation of God, Show me what those besides Him have created. Nay! The unjust are in a manifest straying.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا لُقْمٰنَ الْحِكْمَةَ اَنِ اشْكُرْ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يَّشْكُرْ فَاِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِىٌّ حَمِيْدٌ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA LUQMAANA HIKMATA SAALEHAN ASHKUR LIL-LAAH WA MAN YYASHKUR FA-INNAMAA YASHKORO LENAFSEHI WA MAN KAFARA FA-INNAL LAAHA GHANIYYUN HAMEED.\nAnd indeed gave We to Luqman wisdom saying: “Be thou grateful to God; for whoever is grateful, verily he is only grateful for his own self; and whoever is ungrateful, (it is to the discredit of his own self) then verily God is Self-Sufficient, the Most Praised.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ لُقْمٰنُ لِا بْنِهٖ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهٗ يٰبُنَىَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ ؔؕ اِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(13)\nWA IZ QAALA LUQMAANU LEA BNEH WA HOWA YAE’EZUH YAABUNAA LAA TUSHREK BIL-LAAHE INNAL ASH-SHERKA LAZULMUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd when said Luqman unto his son, while he was exhorting unto him: “O’ my son! associate not aught with God for verily associating (aught) with God is the greatest iniquity.\nوَوَصَّيْنَا الْاِنْسٰنَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ‌ۚ حَمَلَتْهُ اُمُّهٗ وَهْنًا عَلٰى وَهْنٍ وَّفِصٰلُهٗ فِىْ عَامَيْنِ اَنِ اشْكُرْ لِىْ وَلِوَالِدَيْكَؕ اِلَىَّ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(14)\nWA AL-AENSAANA INSAANA HAMALATHU AUMMUH WAHNAN A’LAA WAHNIN WWAFESAALUH FEE A’AAMAYNE SAALEHAN ASHKUR LEE WALEWAALEDAYKA ELAYYA MASEER.\nAnd We did enjoin upon man concerning his parents; beareth him his mother in weakness upon weakness and his weaning taketh two years (and) saying: “Be thou grateful unto Me and unto thy parents; (and remember thou that) unto Me is the ultimate return (of all),\nوَاِنْ جَاهَدٰكَ عَلٰٓى اَنْ تُشْرِكَ بِىْ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ۙ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا‌ وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِى الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوْفًا‌ وَّاتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ مَنْ اَنَابَ اِلَىَّ ‌ۚ ثُمَّ اِلَىَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(15)\nWA IN A’LAA AN TUSHREKA BEE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUM FALAA FALAA WASAAHEBHUMAA FIL DUNYAA MAA’ROOFAN WWAATTABEA’ SABEELA MAN AANAABA ELAYYA SUMMA ELAYYA MARJE-O’KUM FA-ONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd if they contend with thee that thou should associate with Me what thou hast no knowledge of, (then thou) obey them not, and consort kindly, with them in the world, and follow thou the path of him who turneth (repentant) unto Me; then unto Me is the return of ye (all), and then will I inform you of what ye were doing.\nيٰبُنَىَّ اِنَّهَاۤ اِنْ تَكُ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِّنْ خَرْدَلٍ فَتَكُنْ فِىْ صَخْرَةٍ اَوْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ اَوْ فِى الْاَرْضِ يَاْتِ بِهَا اللّٰهُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَطِيْفٌ خَبِيْرٌ‏(16)\nYAABUNAA INNAHAA IN TAKU MISQAALA HABBATIN MIN KHARDALIN FA TAKUN FEE SAKHRATIN AW FIL SAMAAWAATE AW FIL ARZE TAKOONOO BEHAA LAAHO INNAL LAAHA LATEEFUN KHABEERUM.\nO’ my son! Verily if it is even the very weight of the grain of a mustard seed (closed) in (even) a rock, or (be it high above) in the heavens or (buried deep) in the earth, God will bring it (forth) to light; (for) verily God is All-Subtle, All- Aware.\nيٰبُنَىَّ اَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاْمُرْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَانْهَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَاۤ اَصَابَكَ‌ؕ اِنَّ ذٰلِكَ مِنْ عَزْمِ الْاُمُوْرِ‌ۚ ‏(17)\nYAABUNAA AAQEME SALAATA WAAMUR BIL-MA’ROOF WAANHA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WAS BIR A’LAA MAA AASAABAKA INNAL ZAALEKA MIN A’AZME AL-AUMOORE.\nO’ my son! establish prayer and enjoin the good and forbid the evil, and be patient against what befalleth thee; verily this is the task of steadfastness\nوَلَا تُصَعِّرْ خَدَّكَ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَمْشِ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَحًا ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخْتَالٍ فَخُوْرٍۚ‏(18)\nWA LAA TUSAEE’ER KHADDAKA LIN-NAASE WA LAA TAMSHE FIL ARZE MARAHAN INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL KULLA MUKHTAALIN FAKHOORIN.\nAnd turn not thy face at people (in scorn) and walk not in the earth exulting; verily God loveth not any self-conceited boaster\nوَاقْصِدْ فِىْ مَشْيِكَ وَاغْضُضْ مِنْ صَوْتِكَ‌ؕ اِنَّ اَنْكَرَ الْاَصْوَاتِ لَصَوْتُ الْحَمِيْرِ‏(19)\nWAAQSED FEE MASHYEKA WAAGHZUZ MIN SAWTEKA INNAL AANKARA AL-AASWAATE LASAWTU AL-HAMEERE.\nAnd be moderate (in thy movement) and lower thy voice: Note the degree of humility Islam enjoins upon its adherents verily the most unpleasant of voices is the braying of the asses.\nاَلَمْ تَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاَسْبَغَ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعَمَهٗ ظَاهِرَةً وَّبَاطِنَةً ‌ؕ وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّجَادِلُ فِى اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّلَا هُدًى وَّلَا كِتٰبٍ مُّنِيْرٍ‏(20)\nALAM TARAWA ANNAL LAAHA SAKKHARA LAKUM MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WAASBAGHA A’LAYKUM NEA’AMAH ZAAHERATAN WWABAATENATAN WA MENAN NAASE MAN YYUJAADELU FIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WA LAA HODAM WA LAA KETAABIM MMUNEERIN.\nWhat! See ye not that God hath made subservient unto you what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and completed on you His bounties (both) apparently and hidden? yet among the people is he who disputeth concerning God without knowledge and without any guidance and without any book illuminating.\nوَ اِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اتَّبِعُوْا مَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ قَالُوْا بَلْ نَتَّبِعُ مَا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا ؕ اَوَلَوْ كَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ يَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلٰى عَذَابِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(21)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUL TABE-O’O MAAA ANZALAL LAAHO QAALOO BAL NATTA-BE-O’ MAA WAJADNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA LAW KAANA SHAYTAANO YADU’OOHUM ELAA A’ZAABIN SA-E’ER.\nAnd when it is said unto them, “Follow ye what God hath sent down,” say they, “Nay! follow we that on which found we our fathers”; What! (would they do it) even if it be Satan beckoning them unto the chastisement of the blazing fire!\nوَمَنْ يُّسْلِمْ وَجْهَهٗۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقٰى‌ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(22)\nWA MAN YYUSLEM WAJHAHU ELAL LAAHE WA HOWA MOHSENUN FAQADEH TAMSAKA BIL-U’RWATIL AL-WUSQAA WA ELAL LAAHE A’AQEBATUL AL-AUMOORE.\nAnd whosoever setteth his face (submitting himself) unto God, and he be a doer of good, then indeed hath (he) laid hold on a firmest hand-hold (a rope); and unto God is the end of all affairs.\nوَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ كُفْرُهٗ ؕ اِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُهُمْ فَنُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(23)\nWA MAN KAFARA FALAA YAHZUNKA KUFROH ELAYNAA MARJEU’UHUM FANUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nAnd whoever disbelieveth, let not his disbelief grieve thee; unto Us is their return, then will We inform them of what they did; verily God well-knoweth what is in their breasts.\nنُمَتِّعُهُمْ قَلِيْلًا ثُمَّ نَضْطَرُّهُمْ اِلٰى عَذَابٍ غَلِيْظٍ‏(24)\nNUMATTEU’UHUM QALEELAA SUMMA NAZTARRUHUM ELAA A’ZAABIN GHALEEZ.\nWe provide them to enjoy a little, then will We drive them to a severe chastisement.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ قُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‌ ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(25)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAHO QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd if thou askest them “Who created the heavens and the earth?” certainly will they say: “God.” Say thou: “(all) praise is God’s;” “Nay! most of them know not.\nلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْغَنِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(26)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ INNAL LAAHA HOWA AL-GHANEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nGod’s is whatever is in the heavens and the earth; verily God is the Self-Sufficient, the Most Praised.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ شَجَرَةٍ اَقْلَامٌ وَّالْبَحْرُ يَمُدُّهٗ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ سَبْعَةُ اَبْحُرٍ مَّا نَفِدَتْ كَلِمٰتُ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(27)\nWA LAW ANNAL MAA FIL ARZE MIN SHAJARATIN AAQLAAMUN WWAALBAHRU YAMUDDUH MIN BA’DEHI SABA’ATU AABHURIN MAA NAFEDAT KALEMAATU LAAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAnd if it were that all the trees in the earth be pens, and the sea added to seven (more) seas (be ink), (yet) will exhaust not the words of God; Verily God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.\nمَا خَلْقُكُمْ وَلَا بَعْثُكُمْ اِلَّا كَنَفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(28)\nMAA KHALQUKUM WA LAA BAA’SUKUM ILLAA KA-NAFSIM WWAAHEDATIN INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nNeither your creation nor your raising (after your death) is anything but as a single soul: Verily God is All-Hearing, All- Seeing.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُوْلِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَيُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْۤ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(29)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YOOLEJU LAYLA FIL AN-NAHAARE WAYOOLEJU NAHAARA FIL LAYLE SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA ELAA ELAA AJALIM WA ANNAL LAAHA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nSeest thou not that God causeth the night to pass into the day, and causeth the day to pass into the night, and hath made subservient the sun and the moon, each passing an appointed term, and that God, of what ye do, is All-Aware.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنَّ مَا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِ الْبَاطِلُ ۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(30)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO WA ANNAL MAA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHE BAATELO WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA A’LIYYUL AL-KABEERU.\nThis, because God is truth, and that which they call upon besides Him is falsehood, and that God, He is the Highest, the Greatest.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ الْفُلْكَ تَجْرِىْ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِنِعْمَتِ اللّٰهِ لِيُرِيَكُمْ مِّنْ اٰيٰتِهٖؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍ‏(31)\nALAM TARA ANNAL AL-FULKA TAJREE FIL BAHRE BENEA’MATE LAAHE LEEREEKUM MIN AAAYAATEH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nSeest thou not that the ships sail on the sea by the favour of God, that He may show you of His signs? Verily in this are signs for every steadfast grateful (one).\nوَاِذَا غَشِيَهُمْ مَّوْجٌ كَالظُّلَلِ دَعَوُا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ ۙ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮهُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ فَمِنْهُمْ مُّقْتَصِدٌ ‌ؕ وَمَا يَجْحَدُ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلَّا كُلُّ خَتَّارٍ كَفُوْرٍ‏(32)\nWA EZAA GHASHEEHUM MMAWJUN KAALZZULALE DA-A’WUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA FALAMMAA NAJJAAHUM ELAL BARRE FA-MINHUM MMUQTASEDUN WA MAA YAJHADO BE-AAYAATENAA ILLAA KULLO KHATTAARIN KAFOORIN.\nAnd when covereth them a wave like mountains they call upon God in sincere devotion unto Him; but when He bringeth them safe to land, of them are those who halt between (the right and wrong); and disputeth not about Our signs but every perfidious, ungrateful one.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمْ وَاخْشَوْا يَوْمًا لَّا يَجْزِىْ وَالِدٌ عَنْ وَّلَدِهٖ وَلَا مَوْلُوْدٌ هُوَ جَازٍ عَنْ وَّالِدِهٖ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ‌ فَلَا تَغُرَّنَّكُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَلَا يَغُرَّنَّكُمْ بِاللّٰهِ الْغَرُوْرُ‏(33)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO TAQOO TAQUL WAAKHSHAWA YAWMAN LAA YAJZEAA WAALEDUN A’N WWALADEH WA LAA MAWLOODUL HOWA JAAZIN A’N WWAALEDEH SHAY-ANW INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN FALAA TAGHURRANNAKUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA WA LAA YAGHURRANNAKUM BIL-LAAHE AL-GHAROORU.\nO’ ye people! guard ye (your selves against the wrath of) your Lord and dread ye the day when a father shall avail not of his son, neither the child shall avail of its father; verily the promise of God is true, so let not the life of the world beguile you; nor let the deceiver deceive you concerning God.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ‌ ۚ وَيُنَزِّلُ الْغَيْثَ‌ ۚ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِى الْاَرْحَامِ‌ ؕ وَمَا تَدْرِىْ نَفْسٌ مَّاذَا تَكْسِبُ غَدًا‌ ؕ وَّمَا تَدْرِىْ نَفْسٌۢ بِاَىِّ اَرْضٍ تَمُوْتُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ خَبِيْرٌ ‏(34)\nINNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU I’LMUS AS-SAAA’ATE WAYUNAZZELU AL-GHAYSA YA’LAMO MAA FIL AL-AARHAAME WA MAA LAA NAFSUN MMAAZAA TAKSEBU GHADAN WA MAA LAA NAFSUN BE-AYYE AARZIN TAMOOTU INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM KHABEERUM.\nVerily, God is He with Whom is the knowledge of the Hour and He sendeth down the rain, and knoweth He what is in the wombs; and knoweth not any soul what he shall earn the morrow; and knoweth not any soul in what lands he shall die; Verily God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.",
  "merits": "Surah Luqman\nThis Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 34 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if Surah Luqman is recited at night, then angels protect the reciter from Iblees and his army until the next morning, and if recited in the daytime then the angels protect from them him until night time.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will be raised on the Day of Judgement with Hazrat Luqman (a.s.) and will get the reward which is ten times the amount of people who have advised others to do good (amr bil ma’roof) and prevented them from doing bad (nahy a’nil munkar).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has also said that writing this Surah and then putting it in water to dissolve and then drinking the water provides for a cure from all types of illnesses and pains."
}
